@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1617corr-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1617corr-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 16 and 17 corrections"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1617corr-lineage/1.0.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1617corr_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.0.0 (2026-11-18): Mission stage only (one stage per version). Opened on the owner's choice of 2026-11-18 ('Close; open chapters 16-17 next') after confirming Lineage9 closed LS_Achieved.
ORDINAL AND ONE-AT-A-TIME CHECK: the live register files were read; Lineage9 (chapter 18) is LS_Achieved in register v1_7_0 (pushed) before this lineage opened, so only this lineage runs. The next free ordinal is 10.
VERIFIED GAPS (live files measured 2026-11-18 with cme_material_check v1.0.2 and deck standard 1.1.0, not memory). Chapter 17 (deck 2.1.0, page 9.96.1): 53 of 59 notes outside 60 to 140 words; 1 of 46 titles under 4 words; 1 content slide without one thing to look at; 125 of 125 code checks with a prompt marker; 71 of 71 code frames do not parse; 507 lambda occurrences in the page; 2 of 71 frames not found in the page; deck standard fails D7 and D10. Chapter 16 (deck 2.0.1, page 9.97.0): 48 of 54 notes outside range; 2 of 43 titles short; 1 slide without a visual focus; 124 of 124 prompt markers; 75 of 75 frames do not parse; 5 lambdas in the deck and 274 in the page; 2 of 75 frames not found in the page; deck standard fails D7 and D10. Page test result of both pages under the corrected pipeline not yet measured. Source of the rulings: 09-handovers-out/HANDOVER_session_to_next-session_deck-and-page-rulings_v1_1_0.md (owner, 2026-11-14).
WHY A NEW LINEAGE: Lineage9 is closed and a closed lineage is revived only in extraordinary cases; chapters 16 and 17 are a different closeable slice from chapter 18.
REDUCING REWORK (owner, 2026-11-18): each deck is rebuilt once through the generic chapter builder 2.4.0 from a spec, and each page through the lambda-free A-box maker and page test that chapter 18 passed; the conversion pattern of Lineage9 is reused, not rebuilt. Chapters 9 to 15 and 1 to 8 follow in later narrow lineages."""@en .

ex:ProfileDecl10 a backlog:ProfileDeclaration ;
    rdfs:label "Profile: AAL (agentic adaptive), default"@en ;
    backlog:declaresProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:declaresLevel backlog:Level_L2 ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Default ;
    backlog:hasDeclarationRationale "Same declaration as Lineage3 to Lineage9: work is executed by an LLM agent, no human team; AAL is the default profile for agent-executed work. Level L2 stated plainly." ;
    backlog:declaredAt "2026-11-18T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:reviewDate "2026-11-25"^^xsd:date .

ex:Lineage10 a backlog:Lineage ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 16 and 17 corrections, narrow lineage"@en ;
    backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission10 ; backlog:lineageOrdinal 10 ; backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Opened ;
    backlog:hasProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:followsProfileDeclaration ex:ProfileDecl10 ;
    backlog:continuesFrom ex:Lineage2 ;
    rdfs:comment "ex:Lineage2 (sen0414-slides-lineage namespace) is the closed slides lineage this continues from, as Lineage3 to Lineage9 do."@en .

ex:Mission10 a backlog:Mission ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 16 and 17 decks and pages meet the owner's rulings of 2026-11-14"@en ;
    backlog:missionFor ex:Backlog10 ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "The chapter 17 (PDF and Word Documents) and chapter 16 (SQLite Databases) decks and interactive pages, already released, are corrected so that they meet the six rulings of 2026-11-14 on decks and pages (one thing taught per slide, notes that carry the lecture, a Slide code tab, plain code without prompts, only taught Python, checks and reviews recorded before release), with each chapter's approved content, stories and examples unchanged, reusing the conversion built for chapter 18" ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin "Owner's instruction 2026-11-15 (correct the earlier chapters as urgency), 2026-11-18 ('first the corrections; reduce the rework') and the choice 'Close; open chapters 16-17 next' of 2026-11-18." .
